01:07:27,400 --> 01:07:29,311
He 's still there .

539
01:07:29,400 --> 01:07:33,155
- You 've got to help . - I ... I can 't .

540
01:07:34,360 --> 01:07:35,589
What 's wrong ?

541
01:07:37,360 --> 01:07:38,589
Your eye .

542
01:07:43,400 --> 01:07:45,437
Oh no .

543
01:07:47,960 --> 01:07:50,156
It 's too late .

544
01:07:53,280 --> 01:07:55,430
It 's starting .

545
01:07:57,960 --> 01:08:00,110
I 'm very sorry .

546
01:08:13,080 --> 01:08:15,993
( SHE BREATHES DEEPLY )

547
01:08:17,800 --> 01:08:20,030
JOSEPH : July 28th .

548
01:08:20,160 --> 01:08:22,720
I cut myself this morning .

549
01:08:22,800 --> 01:08:25,314
My finger was nearly severed .

550
01:08:25,400 --> 01:08:28,279
- Without feeling any pain I ... - ( SHE SHOUTS )

551
01:08:28,360 --> 01:08:30,510
I ripped it off at the joint .

552
01:08:30,600 --> 01:08:31,999
I felt nothing at all .

553
01:08:33,080 --> 01:08:35,469
I ... I 've been disintegrating rapidly .

554
01:08:35,560 --> 01:08:37,233
( SHE SOBS )

555
01:08:48,080 --> 01:08:51,277
( SHE SCREAMS )

556
01:08:51,400 --> 01:08:53,710
( SHE RETCHES )

557
01:09:08,240 --> 01:09:10,959
( SHE SOBS )

558
01:09:27,880 --> 01:09:29,553
( SIREN WAILS )

559
01:09:34,160 --> 01:09:37,357
OVER TANNOY : Would you please disperse ?

560
01:09:37,440 --> 01:09:40,034
You are ordered to disperse .

561
01:10:26,560 --> 01:10:28,153
( GROWLING )

562
01:11:14,080 --> 01:11:15,275
Thom ?

563
01:11:26,360 --> 01:11:28,351
Father ?

564
01:11:28,440 --> 01:11:32,877
Arletty , I tried to warn you .

565
01:11:32,960 --> 01:11:37,193
I dragged one of the bodies they killed up on the beach , but you still didn 't leave .

566
01:11:38,480 --> 01:11:40,471
There 's little time left .

567
01:11:40,560 --> 01:11:42,437
You 'll have to go .

568
01:11:43,520 --> 01:11:46,194
Tell people on the outside .

569
01:11:46,280 --> 01:11:48,476
Warn them ...

570
01:11:48,560 --> 01:11:52,110
that what happened 100 years ago is happening again .

571
01:11:52,200 --> 01:11:53,315
What ?

572
01:11:53,400 --> 01:11:54,834
Listen .

573
01:11:56,040 --> 01:11:58,236
Please listen .

574
01:11:59,840 --> 01:12:03,754
He came 100 years ago .

575
01:12:05,400 --> 01:12:07,835
A hunter first saw him .

576
01:12:15,680 --> 01:12:17,239
( HORSE SNICKERS )

577
01:12:36,200 --> 01:12:39,591
JOSEPH : He told the hunter that he had been a minister

578
01:12:39,680 --> 01:12:43,150
and had come over the mountains with the Donner party ,

579
01:12:43,240 --> 01:12:46,153
He passed that horrible winter with them

580
01:12:46,240 --> 01:12:49,312
and saw men commit hideous acts .

581
01:12:50,400 --> 01:12:53,836
He said that he himself had eaten human flesh ,

582
01:12:53,920 --> 01:12:56,912
but had survived because he had faith ,

583
01:12:57,000 --> 01:12:58,832
faith in a new master .

584
01:13:00,280 --> 01:13:02,749
The hunter didn 't understand

585
01:13:04,480 --> 01:13:07,950
when the dark stranger said he was spreading his new religion .

586
01:13:09,800 --> 01:13:11,916
( GUNSHOT )

587
01:13:13,400 --> 01:13:15,198
( HE SCREAMS )

588
01:13:15,280 --> 01:13:17,112
( HORSE NEIGHS )

589
01:13:18,800 --> 01:13:20,916
When they found the hunter

590
01:13:22,640 --> 01:13:27,350
he looked as if he 'd been attacked by some kind of animal ,

591
01:13:27,440 --> 01:13:28,760
half eaten .

592
01:13:30,160 --> 01:13:35,155
As he was dying , he told them of the dark stranger .

593
01:13:35,240 --> 01:13:37,754
And they assumed he was delirious .

594
01:13:37,840 --> 01:13:43,279
When he went into a fit , biting them like a rabid dog , they shot him .

595
01:13:46,360 --> 01:13:49,716
The dark stranger watched the chaos

596
01:13:49,800 --> 01:13:52,155
and he walked into the sea .

597
01:13:52,240 --> 01:13:55,119
And said he would return 100 years later

598
01:13:55,200 --> 01:13:58,830
to a world tired and disillusioned .

599
01:13:58,960 --> 01:14:02,874
A world looking back to old gods

600
01:14:02,960 --> 01:14:05,270
and old dark ways .

601
01:14:05,360 --> 01:14:06,919
Our world .

602
01:14:07,000 --> 01:14:09,276
You 've got to go now .

603
01:14:09,360 --> 01:14:11,192
Most of this town 's infected .

604
01:14:11,280 --> 01:14:15,638
He 's got to be destroyed before the moon turns blood red

605
01:14:15,720 --> 01:14:19,190
and he returns to lead them up the coast and inland into the cities .

606
01:14:19,280 --> 01:14:21,191
We can both go .

607
01:14:21,280 --> 01:14:23,635
( SHE SCREAMS )

608
01:14:27,960 --> 01:14:30,520
They took me

609
01:14:30,600 --> 01:14:32,432
and they did this to me .

610
01:14:32,520 --> 01:14:34,193
Help me .

611
01:14:37,000 --> 01:14:39,799
No ! No !

612
01:14:43,560 --> 01:14:45,119
( HE 3053 )

613
01:14:54,480 --> 01:14:56,630
( HE SHOUTS )

614
01:14:56,720 --> 01:15:01,669
Help me !

615
01:15:04,800 --> 01:15:06,791
Help me !

616
01:15:12,480 --> 01:15:15,598
Help me ! Help me !

617
01:15:46,160 --> 01:15:48,470
Daddy ...

618
01:15:48,560 --> 01:15:50,597
We 'll go home .

619
01:15:52,920 --> 01:15:54,399
I can 't .

620
01:15:54,480 --> 01:15:57,552
I already tested human flesh .

621
01:16:16,440 --> 01:16:19,159
CHARLIE : You got to kill him .

622
01:16:21,840 --> 01:16:25,720
If you love your daddy , you will kill him .

623
01:16:33,480 --> 01:16:35,710
Can 't bury him .

624
01:16:38,880 --> 01:16:40,314
Don 't put him in the ground .

625
01:16:42,360 --> 01:16:44,476
Gotta burn him .

626
01:16:44,560 --> 01:16:46,790
Destroy his body .

627
01:17:02,840 --> 01:17:04,956
Stay back !

628
01:17:45,320 --> 01:17:46,754
Arletty ?

629
01:18:01,680 --> 01:18:03,671
( HE COUGHS )

630
01:18:24,600 --> 01:18:25,795
Arletty ?

631
01:18:25,880 --> 01:18:27,791
( HE COUGHS )

632
01:18:37,160 --> 01:18:39,800
Arletty ?

633
01:19:04,120 --> 01:19:06,157
( SHE SCREAMS )

634
01:19:24,080 --> 01:19:26,640
Why didn 't you leave ?

635
01:19:28,320 --> 01:19:30,516
I came back here to get you .

636
01:19:38,560 --> 01:19:40,358
Thom , it 's too late .

637
01:19:42,560 --> 01:19:43,959
God !

638
01:20:07,960 --> 01:20:09,598
I saw them in town .

639
01:20:11,200 --> 01:20:14,238
They 're traveling in packs , like wolves .

640
01:20:18,680 --> 01:20:20,193
- I think they 'll hold out . - Thom !

641
01:20:38,440 --> 01:20:40,158
I was dreaming .

642
01:20:42,560 --> 01:20:46,713
We were in a forest and it was snowing .

643
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:52,756
The trees were wet and you were looking up .

644
01:20:55,280 --> 01:20:56,953
And I asked you what ...

645
01:20:57,040 --> 01:20:59,156
what you were thinking .

646
01:21:00,400 --> 01:21:05,634
You said you were thinking about all the people who were born and ...

647
01:21:05,760 --> 01:21:08,229
and died

648
01:21:08,320 --> 01:21:11,358
while the trees went on living .

649
01:21:14,320 --> 01:21:15,390
( HE SIGHS )

650
01:21:15,520 --> 01:21:20,640
Then we came to a village and we spent the night in the wood room .

651
01:21:22,600 --> 01:21:28,994
The next day it was so cold we stayed in bed to keep warm .

652
01:22:39,680 --> 01:22:41,000
Thom , help !

653
01:22:45,080 --> 01:22:47,037
Get out , get out .

654
01:23:57,120 --> 01:23:59,953
ARLETTY : We thought we must have made it out of the town .

655
01:24:01,400 --> 01:24:03,550
And then we saw the first one .

656
01:24:20,520 --> 01:24:23,990
They were coming down to the beach as they did every night ,

657
01:24:24,080 --> 01:24:25,798
to stare at the ocean and wait .

658
01:24:36,560 --> 01:24:39,757
We could go no further .

659
01:24:39,840 --> 01:24:42,150
They were all around ...

660
01:24:42,240 --> 01:24:46,632
watching us , staring at us .

661
01:24:46,720 --> 01:24:49,678
As if we were trapped animals ,

662
01:24:49,760 --> 01:24:53,879
caught , already bleeding ,

663
01:24:53,960 --> 01:24:56,839
yet still struggling hopelessly .

664
01:25:09,880 --> 01:25:13,635
We hoped to make it to one of the small boats on the horizon .

665
01:25:13,720 --> 01:25:16,758
And then we would drift out and head for safety down the coast .

666
01:25:18,760 --> 01:25:20,717
He was having trouble with his arm .

667
01:25:22,440 --> 01:25:24,750
I had hurt him .

668
01:25:24,840 --> 01:25:27,229
And now I couldn 't help him .

669
01:25:28,320 --> 01:25:30,880
Boats didn 't seem any nearer .

670
01:25:40,480 --> 01:25:41,550
Thom !

671
01:25:42,960 --> 01:25:44,314
Thom !

672
01:25:45,960 --> 01:25:47,519
Thom !

673
01:25:57,760 --> 01:25:59,114
Thom !

674
01:26:03,760 --> 01:26:05,194
( SHE SCREAMS )

675
01:26:07,760 --> 01:26:10,878
And the last thing I saw was the setting sun .

676
01:26:18,360 --> 01:26:20,078
They hadn 't let me drown .

677
01:26:21,480 --> 01:26:24,359
They had pulled me from the water .

678
01:26:24,440 --> 01:26:26,829
They had prevented my last escape .

679
01:26:28,600 --> 01:26:31,433
That night most of the town was on the beach .

680
01:26:32,520 --> 01:26:34,716
They built their fires ,

681
01:26:34,840 --> 01:26:39,789
not for warmth , but as beacons to be seen from the black ocean .

682
01:26:40,880 --> 01:26:43,235
They dressed me in an old gown .

683
01:26:44,800 --> 01:26:46,552
I was to be offered .

684
01:26:46,640 --> 01:26:49,678
And following their prophecy , the moon turned blood red .

685
01:26:50,840 --> 01:26:52,831
And the dark stranger returned .

686
01:27:07,840 --> 01:27:11,549
He let me go with a story that condemned me ,

687
01:27:11,640 --> 01:27:14,439
knowing that they wouldn 't listen .

688
01:27:14,520 --> 01:27:16,557
He was right .

689
01:27:16,640 --> 01:27:19,792
I made it back and they put me here .

690
01:27:19,880 --> 01:27:23,839
JACOB : He told them of the dark stranger and they assumed he was delirious .

691
01:27:23,920 --> 01:27:29,472
When he went into a fit , biting them like a rabid dog , they shot him .

692
01:27:29,600 --> 01:27:32,274
The night the moon turned blood red ...

693
01:27:32,360 --> 01:27:34,510
CHARLIE : The redder the moon got up there ,

694
01:27:34,600 --> 01:27:37,911
the closer the people were being jerked toward hell .

695
01:27:38,000 --> 01:27:41,277
- Men ... Men could do horrible things . - ( JOSEPH 'S VOICE CONTINUES )

696
01:27:41,360 --> 01:27:45,831
( JOSEPH AND CHARLIE 'S VOICE MINGLE )

697
01:27:45,920 --> 01:27:48,992
( SHE SCREAMS , DROWNING OUT THE VOICES )

698
01:27:49,120 --> 01:27:54,194
( SCREAM ECHOES )

699
01:27:54,280 --> 01:27:56,157
( SCREAM FADES )

700
01:27:56,240 --> 01:27:58,754
ARLETTY : During the day they let me out with the others .

701
01:28:01,240 --> 01:28:05,438
We sit in the sun and wait .

702
01:28:05,520 --> 01:28:08,399
We sleep ...

703
01:28:08,480 --> 01:28:10,073
and we dream .

704
01:28:11,960 --> 01:28:16,750
Each of us dying slowly in the prison of our minds ,

705
01:28:20,640 --> 01:28:22,358
And at night

706
01:28:22,440 --> 01:28:25,239
I roam the empty halls

707
01:28:25,320 --> 01:28:27,630
listening to their whispering

708
01:28:27,720 --> 01:28:30,712
and try to find someone who can hear me

709
01:28:30,800 --> 01:28:32,871
because I have to warn them

710
01:28:32,960 --> 01:28:37,909
that back there in that small town on the coast

711
01:28:38,000 --> 01:28:40,913
they 're growing in number

712
01:28:41,000 --> 01:28:44,994
and moving out into the rest of the world

713
01:28:45,080 --> 01:28:47,549
spreading their sickness

714
01:28:47,680 --> 01:28:52,436
and in order to live they 'll take you one by one

715
01:28:52,560 --> 01:28:55,632
and no one will hear you scream .

716
01:28:56,920 --> 01:29:00,038
No one will hear you SCREAM !

